      <p>These are the starting prices for each trim. Kia sells most trims with more than one engine and gearbox, and the automatic and diesel versions cost more, so price the exact combination you want. The GTX and X-Line pairs cost the same: X-Line is a styling pack with darker trim and black wheels.</p>
      <p>Two changes since launch matter here. Kia added the GTX(O) and X-Line(O) on 1 July 2026, with a fuller driver-assistance suite. And CarWale reported on 20 November 2026 that the turbo-petrol iMT versions have been dropped. Kia has not announced this, but its current brochure lists the turbo-petrol with the 7-speed DCT only. CarWale puts the cheapest turbo-petrol, the HTK(O) DCT, at ₹16.62 lakh ex-showroom.</p>
